  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Africa Catalytic Investment Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Africa Catalytic Investment Facility, a partnership between the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and the Dutch Entrepreneurial Development Bank (FMO), aims to address the critical financing challenges faced by early-stage, impact-driven entrepreneurs in Sub-Saharan Africa (SSA), specifically in Nigeria and Ghana. Many entrepreneurs struggle to access early-stage capital, which limits their ability to scale innovative solutions essential for economic mobility and climate resilience.This project seeks to close this funding gap by providing catalytic funding to nine high-potential impact entrepreneurs. Simultaneously, it will enhance the capacity of Entrepreneur Support Organizations (ESOs) by engaging them in the Due Diligence process, better equipping them to identify and mobilize capital for high-potential startups.This project takes a multi-phase approach to support entrepreneurs at different stages of their journey. The complementary strengths of RVO and FMO will be leveraged to create synergies that enhance access to finance and improve local ecosystems.The project will be implemented by Village Capital in Nigeria and Ghana, regions with significant youth populations and a growing need for innovative economic and climate solutions. Ultimately, the Africa Catalytic Investment Facility aims to strengthen the entrepreneurship ecosystem, stimulate the growth of impactful enterprises, and contribute to sustainable development in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
